   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "scm_step1410_physics_column",
     "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, p_top = 177.6 hPa, data/eqwefic/scm_ref) dumped by the instrumented ctessum-claude/WRF fork (module_esm_dump, commit 592f693) at TWO levels for the same step: the PHYSICS-DRIVER level (hooks around radiation_driver, surface_driver + pbl_driver and the physics-tendency sum in dyn_em/module_first_rk_step_part1.F -- dumps subassembly_all, _pbl and _rad) and the KERNEL level (sfclayrev, sw, ysu and rrtm scm_ref dumps of the same call). The seven dumps are merged into one column namespace by tools/merge_dumps.py (esm_dump_scm_suite_<step>.json, variables tagged all_/pbl_/rad_/sfc_/sw_/ysu_/rrtm_) because tools/fill_tests.py admits two dumps per test; the numbers are transcribed by fill_tests.py from the sidecar couplings/scm_physics_column.esm.fill.json. All references are real32 model values. The DRIVER-level tendency vector (rthblten, rublten, rvblten, rqvblten, rqcblten, rqiblten, rthraten, rth_phys_sum, hfx, qfx, gsw, glw, olr, pblh) is the contract this document exists to pin: it is what WRF hands to the dynamics, and rqcblten/rqiblten are asserted here for the first time. Regime: WRF step 1410 (kernel call 2820), 18:29 UTC = 12:02 local solar time -- the strongest daytime forcing of the 24 h reference run: gsw = 549.7 W/m^2 (cos zenith 0.639), glw = 268.9, olr = 256.0, slab hfx = 173.6 W/m^2 (SfclayRev's own 173.5), Ri_b = -0.118 (regime 4, free convection), u* = 0.454 m/s, h = 926 m over 16 layers, tsk = 288.5 K, and only a trace of cirrus aloft (qi <= 2.1e-9, three cloudy layers), so YSU's cloud-top entrainment branch is inactive and no liquid cloud is present. Residuals of the whole assembly against the step-1410 references, measured with zero tolerances: surface-layer outputs <= 1.9e-6 relative (rmol; hfx 5.4e-7, u* 4.0e-8, qsfc / z0 / regime exact), PBL height 6.4e-7 relative and kpbl exact, K_h / K_m Linf 2.3e-4 / 1.6e-4 m^2/s, longwave fluxes Linf 2.3e-4 (F_up) and 1.3e-4 W/m^2 (F_dn), dthdt_lw and rthraten 5.2e-9 K/s, dthdt_sw 1.6e-10 K/s, gsw 1.4e-6, glw 2.4e-7 and olr 3.2e-7 relative, and the PBL tendencies 1.40e-6 K/s (dthdt, column max 3.7e-4), 3.79e-7 and 4.68e-7 m/s^2 (dudt / dvdt, max 3.4e-4 / 3.2e-4), 2.14e-10 1/s (dqvdt, max 3.3e-7), dqcdt exactly zero (no cloud water) and dqidt 2.41e-23 (max 1.3e-16) -- all against the dt -> 0 reference described next, which is where those five numbers came down from 1.1e-4, 6.1e-5, 3.0e-5, 1.4e-8 and 1.5e-18. The PBL TENDENCIES are asserted against the dt -> 0 LIMIT of the YSU kernel, which is what this document computes, and NOT against WRF's driver-level rthblten/rublten/rvblten/rqvblten/rqcblten/rqiblten: those are the IMPLICIT tridiagonal step's (c_new - c_old)/dt at dt = 60 s, which is not an instantaneous derivative and differs from one by 2-31 % in this column (measured, TENDENCY_ERROR_BUDGET.md). The reference is the second-order Richardson extrapolation (8 T(dt/4) - 6 T(dt/2) + T(dt))/3 of real64 replays of THIS step's dumped YSU column through kernels/ysu_driver of the ctessum-claude/WRF fork at dt = 0.04/0.02/0.01 s (data/eqwefic/dumps/ysu/scmref_2820_dt*.json, transcribed by tools/reref_pbl_dt0.py) -- the same reference components/atmospheric_dynamics/ysu/ysu.esm's own tests already use, and the reason they pass at abs 1e-9 while this document used to need abs 1e-3. The kernel carries NEED_B4B_DURING_CCPP_TESTING = 1, so ttnp is a TEMPERATURE tendency and the theta reference is ttnp/pi2d (FORTRAN_BUGS N1). The extrapolation is self-consistent to 1.0e-9 (utnp) and 5.6e-8 (ttnp) of the column maximum when recomputed from dt = 0.08/0.04/0.02. Re-referencing dropped the measured residuals by two to three orders of magnitude and the tolerances follow it: pbl_dthdt 1.14e-4 -> 1.40e-6 K/s (abs 1e-3 -> 1e-5), pbl_dudt 6.15e-5 -> 3.79e-7 m/s^2 (abs 5e-4 -> 2e-6), pbl_dvdt 2.96e-5 -> 4.68e-7 m/s^2 (abs 2e-4 -> 2e-6), pbl_dqvdt 1.41e-8 -> 2.14e-10 1/s (abs 1e-7 -> 1e-9), pbl_dqidt 1.52e-18 -> 2.41e-23 1/s (abs 1e-17 -> 1e-22), rth_phys_sum 1.13e-4 -> 1.40e-6 K/s (abs 1e-3 -> 1e-5), dtheta_m_dt_phys 1.13e-4 -> 1.48e-6 K/s (abs 1e-3 -> 1e-5), dtheta_m_conv_delta 6.60e-6 -> 9.94e-8 K/s (abs 2e-5 -> 5e-7). rth_phys_sum, dtheta_m_dt_phys and dtheta_m_conv_delta contain a PBL term and are re-formed from the same limit. What is left is the geometry/real32 floor the surface layer shows, not a scheme error. The driver-level th2/t2/q2 are overwritten by the land-surface branch of surface_driver, so those three are referenced to the kernel-level sfclayrev dump, and the slab's driver-level hfx/qfx are prescribed (hfx_lsm/qfx_lsm) because the land scheme is not co-mounted -- see the model description. TOLERANCES: each is the smallest of {1, 2, 5} x 10^k that is at least 5x the residual measured in a zero-tolerance run (relative for the scalars, absolute for the Linf_error column assertions), with a 1e-6 relative floor; an assertion that is exact at zero tolerance keeps abs 0. SLAB COUPLING (2026-09-12): the slab land surface is co-mounted (EarthSciAST #213 index_set_rename gives its 4-cell soil column the axis name soil/soil_nodes, so it no longer collides with the 59-layer atmospheric lev), fed by Sfc.flhc/flqc and by this step's Sw.gsw and Heat.glw -- the dumped pbl_gsw/pbl_glw are bit-identical to sw_gsw/rrtm_glw, so radiation_driver's own output is what surface_driver saw -- and its hfx/qfx now drive YSU instead of the values prescribed from the dump. The slab's esm form is an INSTANTANEOUS flux calculator, while WRF's SLAB sub-steps the soil and reports the flux at the END of its internal step (FORTRAN_BUGS N12), so the coupled fluxes sit a measured 7.5e-4 (hfx), 3.1e-4 (qfx, lh) and 1.8e-4 (qsfc) below the driver-level hfx_out/qfx_out/lh_out/qsfc_out they are asserted against; the tolerances above are that gap, not a solver floor, and the component's instantaneous values themselves are pinned to 2e-5 against a dt = 0.01 s real64 slab_driver replay in couplings/surface_soil_column.esm. Because YSU now sees the instantaneous flux, its exchange coefficients move by Linf 0.042 m^2/s (K_h, 2.4e-4 of the 176.8 column maximum) and 0.025 (K_m, 2.4e-4 of 102.6), which is why those two tolerances are 0.06 and 0.04 rather than 0.002 and 0.001. lsm_capg and lsm_land still match exactly. WSM6 remains un-mounted: its stages are in-place state increments, not rates (see the document description). USE_THETA_M CONVERSION (added 2026-09-17, PLAN.md 3.1 item (1)). WRFMoistThetaTendency (components/atmospheric_dynamics/wrf_arw/moist_theta_tendency.esm, conv_t_tendf_to_moist) is mounted here and driven by the assembly's OWN outputs: rth_phys_sum, the summed radiative-plus-PBL dry-theta tendency, goes into its dtheta_dt_phys_in and YSU's rqvblten into its dqv_dt_phys_in, through the mount-edge library couplings/tests/physics_couple_thetam_inputs.esm. Its other two inputs, theta_m and moist_old(P_qv), keep coming from the conv_t_tendf_to_moist dump (data/eqwefic/scm_solthm, fork 1b4b556): they are the DYNAMICAL state at the point of the RK step where the conversion runs, which this physics-only assembly does not carry. Reconstructing theta_m as theta(1 + R_v/R_d q_v) from YSU's own inputs instead was measured and REJECTED -- it differs from the dumped theta_m by up to 0.0178 K, which moves the converted tendency by up to 9.4e-9 K/s through the vapour term, ten times the 1e-9 bound below. TWO assertions, and their tolerances are set by the assembly's KNOWN PBL gap, not by the conversion. dtheta_m_dt_phys is bounded at Linf abs 1e-5 K/s -- the same bound rth_phys_sum itself carries in this document -- because it inherits that quantity's residual: measured 1.48e-6 K/s once the PBL term is referenced to the dt -> 0 limit (it was 1.13e-4 K/s against WRF's implicit rthblten increment). The component's own test pins the conversion arithmetic at abs 1e-9 on dumped inputs, so nothing is lost. What CAN be pinned tightly here is what the conversion ADDS, dtheta_m_conv_delta = dtheta_m_dt_phys - rth_phys_sum: the PBL theta gap largely cancels in the difference, and the residual falls to 6.58e-6 K/s (bound abs 2e-5, 3x). That 6.58e-6 is not the conversion's: it is 1.6084 x 289 K x 1.4e-8 1/s, i.e. the assembly's own rqvblten residual carried through the (R_v/R_d) theta dq_v/dt term, plus 8.7e-7 from the theta term. The conversion is not cosmetic: at this step dtheta_m_conv_delta reaches 1.54e-4 K/s (RMS 2.51e-5), 40 % of rth_phys_sum's own 3.80e-4 maximum, almost all of it the vapour term.",
